{"name":"Mountain Dew","hex":"#cfe2e0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mountain Dew","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A brand of citrus-flavored, carbonated, heavily caffeinated beverage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mountain_Dew"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mountain Dew","blocks":[{"text":"Mountain Dew, stylized as Mtn Dew in some countries and colloquially known as Dew in some areas, is a soft drink brand owned by PepsiCo. The original formula was invented in 1940 by Tennessee beverage bottlers Barney and Ally Hartman. A revised formula was created by Bill Bridgforth in 1958. The rights to this formula were obtained by the Tip Corporation of Marion, Virginia. William H. \"Bill\" Jones of the Tip Corporation further refined the formula, launching that version of Mountain Dew in 1961. In August 1964, the Mountain Dew brand and production rights were acquired from Tip by the Pepsi-Cola company, and the distribution expanded across the United States and Canada."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Mountain_Dew_2025_logo.svg/330px-Mountain_Dew_2025_logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Dew","wikidata":"Q896"},{"title":"Mountain Dew (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Mountain Dew is a lost 1917 American silent comedy-drama film directed by Thomas N. Heffron and starring Margery Wilson. It was produced and distributed by the Triangle Film Corporation."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain_Dew_(film)","wikidata":"Q16665406"},{"title":"Mountain","blocks":[{"text":"A mountain is an elevated portion of the surface of a planet, generally with steep sides that show significant exposed bedrock. Although there are no universally accepted definitions, a mountain is usually considered higher than a hill. By definition, mountains are often thought of as being a landform which is higher than 2,000 feet (610 m). It may either have a limited summit area or be a smaller plateau with high elevation and steep sides. A few mountains are isolated summits, but most occur in mountain ranges."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg/330px-Everest_North_Face_toward_Base_Camp_Tibet_Luca_Galuzzi_2006.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mountain","wikidata":"Q8502"},{"title":"Dew","blocks":[{"text":"Dew is water in the form of droplets that appears on thin, exposed objects in the morning or evening due to condensation. \nAs the exposed surface cools by radiating its heat, atmospheric moisture condenses at a rate greater than that at which it can evaporate, resulting in the formation of water droplets."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/A_drop_of_dew_on_a_clover.jpg/330px-A_drop_of_dew_on_a_clover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dew","wikidata":"Q41097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Mountain_dew_1.jpg/500px-Mountain_dew_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Mountain_dew_1.jpg/1280px-Mountain_dew_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Mountain_dew_1.jpg/500px-Mountain_dew_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMountain_dew_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/5d/Mountain_Dew_sign_Tonto_Arizona.jpg/500px-Mountain_Dew_sign_Tonto_Arizona.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedi